  message: "PR #2183 fixes the display and metadata half and leaves this item OPEN for the identity half. DONE: the displayed signature, meta.parameters types and a class attribute's signature come from ast.unparse (Callable[[int, str], None], Literal[-1, 1], Annotated[int, max(1, 2)]); 'Callable[, ' in the 20-repository run is 0 after (3 repositories before); stable_id and id of the fixture functions are byte-identical before and after. NOT DONE, OWNER DECISION: the signature hashed into stable_id still comes from _format_annotation with its holes; test_py_annotation_rendering.py pins that text. Options: correct it inside unreleased v14, or as a later bump, or leave it. A count of affected functions on a corpus has not been made. base_classes with a call-expression base stays [''] by design (WI-pusan). Found while testing, filed: WI-tirob-jabav-mosis-kiluh-farih-dimoj-hisah-huliz (meta.parameters omits positional-only and keyword-only parameters)."  # f4ce
