  message: "PR #2200, 2026-11-16: the IDENTITY half is done, by the 11-15 ruling (fill the holes only, the renderer is not replaced). Re-ran the review's pair: `C.m(self, cb: Callable[[int], None])` and `C.m(self, cb: Callable[[bytes, str], None])` shared sha256:9dd356b6146f0eae on dev and have two ids now (digests 1c148707a0e85277 and a90ac88cea755790); the hashed text went from `(self, cb: Callable[, None]) -> None` to `(self, cb: Callable[[int], None]) -> None`. THE TWO CHECKS THIS ITEM STILL OWED ARE DONE: (1) the count on a corpus beyond this repo: sqlalchemy 70 of 55,790 Python symbols moved (0.13%), fastapi's package 14 of 687 (2.04%), poetry src 10 of 1,902; every symbol without a hole kept its id. (2) the same question for the other analyzers: asked of all of them; the hole existed in Java, Kotlin, Swift, Go, C#, PHP, Scala, Dart and Groovy and is fixed in each in this PR (owner 11-16), with the shared helpers' losses and the missing type parameters filed. STATUS LEFT AS IT IS, because two forms the TITLE names still hold: `class P(namedtuple(...))` gives meta.base_classes == [''] on both arms (kept by design under WI-pusan), and decorator names / decorator-argument values still go through the default `_format_annotation` (fill_holes=False), which writes '' for a node it has no case for; the decorator text is a hash input. Also still not in the hashed text: the `/` and `*` markers, *args / **kwargs annotations, PEP 695 parameters, tuple[()] (filed). OWNER: close this on the identity half and move the base-class and decorator forms to their own item, or keep it open for them; I did not choose. Repro record (both arms, commands and copied outputs): ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/stable_id_items_review_11152026/pr2/tracker/repros.md; per-package detail: pr2/STATUS.md; churn: pr2/final_measure.txt."  # c466
