  message: "OWNER RULING 2026-11-16: close this item on the identity work; the two leftover forms go to their own item, WI-bosor-jidud-sahib-luhap-latot-duzid-hanoh-lotam. DONE (PR #2200, stableid v15): annotations that differ only inside a form the renderer had no case for no longer share a stable id (the review's pair `Callable[[int], None]` / `Callable[[bytes, str], None]`: one id on dev 3da1f85b37, two on the PR's code); corpus count beyond this repo: sqlalchemy 70 of 55,790 Python symbols moved, fastapi's package 14 of 687, poetry src 10 of 1,902; the same question was asked of every other analyzer and the hole fixed in Java, Kotlin, Swift, Go, C#, PHP, Scala, Dart and Groovy. Display and meta.parameters were fixed earlier (PR #2183). NOT DONE, now on WI-bosor-jidud-sahib-luhap-latot-duzid-hanoh-lotam: `class P(namedtuple(...))` still gives base_classes == [''], and an attribute decorator on a call (`@a().b`) is named `.b`. CORRECTION to my note of earlier today on this item: it said the decorator text is a hash input. It is not. The stable id hashes decorator NAMES through `_extract_py_decorator_names` (plain names only), which does not use `_format_annotation`; the holes are in decorator metadata only, and fixing them moves no id. Leftovers in the HASHED signature (`/` and `*` markers, *args / **kwargs annotations, PEP 695 parameters, tuple[()]) are on WI-gikif-sipon-dotor-lipit-mibas-fafum-bulir-molal. Repro record: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/stable_id_items_review_11152026/pr2/tracker/repros.md section 7."  # a90a
